{"author":{"id":"337a442880d7106d509ff84f2f7fef51acce8bce88b081d4f4c3f0298b7e7941"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1791836100,"nonce":"qRYE4F08EhSC3yCFhiiSuoln7vs=","message":"Decision: parallelism uses a small ThreadPoolExecutor with one sqlite connection per worker thread (like console apply_bg), not fanout.run_ordered from PR 182. Reason: resolve_group reads and writes the DB mid-walk, so a shared connection would need the lock around the walk; order of results does not matter here. Per-host limits and robots stay in FetchContext. In-memory DBs and injected ctx factories run serially. New settings apply_links.per_run (200, 0 = off) and apply_links.workers (4).","files":null}]}